# Nougat extraction stub — Peruzzo et al. 2014 (VQE, photonic)

**Paper:** A. Peruzzo, J. McClean, P. Shadbolt, M.-H. Yung, X.-Q. Zhou, P. J. Love,
A. Aspuru-Guzik, J. L. O'Brien. "A variational eigenvalue solver on a photonic
quantum processor." *Nature Communications* **5**, 4213 (2014).
arXiv:1304.3061.

## Status

This is a stub. The original replication run used a plain-text `paper.md`
extract of the arXiv PDF as its reading substrate. A full Nougat pass
(equation-preserving markdown extraction) was not run at replication time and
was not run at this backfill.

## Known missing artifact

**Supplementary Table 2 (tapered 2-qubit Hamiltonian).** The paper's absolute
energies are reported in MJ/mol against a specific tapered 2-qubit qubit-space
Hamiltonian given in Supp. Table 2. This table is not in the parsed `paper.md`
and its absence is the source of the absolute-energy-zero convention gap
documented in the report. A future Nougat pass over the supplementary PDF
would recover this table and enable an absolute-energy comparison.

## What was used instead

- Text-only extract of the main manuscript to identify: the algorithm (VQE),
  the molecule (HeH+), the optimizer (Nelder-Mead), the hardware-noise headline
  (96% within chemical accuracy), and the equilibrium bond length
  (R_eq = 92.3 +/- 0.1 pm).
- The molecule specification was independently constructed via
  PennyLane `qml.qchem.molecular_hamiltonian` at STO-3G, not read from the paper.

## Follow-up

If a proper Nougat extraction is added later, deposit the full `.mmd` here and
extract Supp. Table 2 into `extraction/tapered_hamiltonian.json` so a matched
absolute-energy comparison becomes possible.
